<urn:atm:triage:finding/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT" ;
  triage:title "split Sent/Acknowledged test contract duplicated across three patterns: 2 helper-pair definitions + 6 direct-match sites" ;
  triage:description "Test code in crates/atm-daemon/src/tests_post_send_graft_warning.rs (lines 50, 55) defines expect_sent_response() and expect_ack_response() helpers. Identical helpers duplicated with pub(super) visibility in crates/atm-daemon/src/tests/runtime_root/mod.rs (lines 48, 53, 63: expect_sent_response, sent_response_ref, expect_ack_response). Additionally, peer_transport/tests/harness.rs has 6 sites (lines 110, 161, 286, 409, 529, 686) where the ResponseEnvelope::Send(SendResponseEnvelope::Sent(...)) pattern is matched directly inline instead of using helpers. All three patterns maintain exhaustive matching on SendResponseEnvelope::Sent and SendResponseEnvelope::Acknowledged. This is the test-code counterpart to AG18-QA-004, which identified the same pattern in production code (composition.rs and atm-graft/src/lib.rs). The test code duplication requires a single shared helper module or trait to consolidate the split match logic into one canonical location." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:category "test-code-structure" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-19T22:31:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT/pAG-s21/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT/pAG-s21/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT/pAG-s21/3> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT/pAG-s21/4> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT/pAG-s21/5> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT/pAG-s21/6> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT/pAG-s21/7> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT/pAG-s21/8> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT/pAG-s21/9> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s21/bf96dc86> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAG-s21/bf96dc86> ;
  triage:notes "AG21-QA-2 recheck on feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing @ bf96dc86: QA-1 identified 2-way duplication (two independent helper-pair definitions). QA-2 recheck now confirms 3-way duplication, worsened: both helper-pair definitions remain active PLUS 6 additional direct-match sites in peer_transport/tests/harness.rs where the split pattern is matched inline without using any helper. This indicates the duplication pattern is more pervasive than initially triaged. Occurrence nodes 1-2 (tests_post_send_graft_warning.rs, lines 50 and 55) and 3 (tests/runtime_root/mod.rs, lines 48/53/63 consolidated) remain from QA-1; occurrences 4-9 document the 6 direct-match sites in harness.rs (lines 110, 161, 286, 409, 529, 686) newly identified in QA-2. All on s21; branches s18-s20 do not have these test helpers, s22-s25 pinned at baseline. Correlation: AG18-QA-004 addresses production Sent/Acknowledged split (composition.rs, atm-graft); SPLIT-TEST-CONTRACT addresses test code. dispatchReady remains true; worsened duplication does not change dispatch readiness, only fix scope." .

